WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:02.669
Southwest Airlines melting down

00:00:02.670 --> 00:00:03.629
in the wake of the Christmas

00:00:03.630 --> 00:00:04.289
holiday.

00:00:04.290 --> 00:00:06.239
One of the worst airline meltdowns.

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:07.349
Travel nightmare.

00:00:07.350 --> 00:00:08.159
Unprecedented.

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:08.729
Chaos.

00:00:08.730 --> 00:00:08.835
Chaos.

00:00:08.836 --> 00:00:09.836
Chaos.

00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:10.919
It's crazy.

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:12.629
When Southwest Airlines underwent a

00:00:12.630 --> 00:00:14.249
historic meltdown during the

00:00:14.250 --> 00:00:16.649
Christmas travel season and canceled

00:00:16.650 --> 00:00:19.109
nearly 17,000 flights,

00:00:19.110 --> 00:00:21.389
politicians pounced like passengers

00:00:21.390 --> 00:00:23.369
on a second bag of free peanuts.

00:00:23.370 --> 00:00:24.539
Well, they need to take care of

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:26.009
their passengers and they need to

00:00:26.010 --> 00:00:27.659
take care of their employees.

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:29.759
It's an unacceptable situation.

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:31.769
But what about the FAA?

00:00:31.770 --> 00:00:33.299
When its Notice to Air Mission

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:35.099
system, which gives pilots

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:37.169
information about flights, crashed

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:39.089
due to a corrupted file,

00:00:39.090 --> 00:00:41.159
the agency halted all domestic

00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:43.439
air travel, triggering 1,700

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:45.569
cancellations and 9,000

00:00:45.570 --> 00:00:47.369
delays that screwed up air travel

00:00:47.370 --> 00:00:48.359
for days.

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:50.279
Secretary Buttigieg has pledged to

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:51.659
get to the bottom of it all and

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:53.819
update the system with the single

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:55.739
mindedness of a TSA agent

00:00:55.740 --> 00:00:58.109
confiscating your toenail clippers.

00:00:58.110 --> 00:00:59.609
We'll be approaching Congress,

00:00:59.610 --> 00:01:00.899
indicating the resources and

00:01:00.900 --> 00:01:02.309
strategy that we think we need for

00:01:02.310 --> 00:01:03.959
the next five years to make sure

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:05.458
that FAA has everything that they

00:01:05.459 --> 00:01:07.739
need in terms of systems, resources

00:01:07.740 --> 00:01:08.609
and staff.

00:01:08.610 --> 00:01:10.469
Don't expect much to happen any time

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:12.329
soon. Minnesota Congressman

00:01:12.330 --> 00:01:14.219
Pete Stauber introduced legislation

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:15.629
to modernize the Notice to Air

00:01:15.630 --> 00:01:17.939
Mission system in 2019

00:01:17.940 --> 00:01:19.769
and 2021, but it

00:01:19.770 --> 00:01:21.209
ultimately went nowhere.

00:01:21.210 --> 00:01:22.889
And when it comes to the air-traffic

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:24.719
control system that actually governs

00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:26.579
all takeoffs and landings, the

00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:28.529
FAA is about two decades

00:01:28.530 --> 00:01:30.419
behind other countries when

00:01:30.420 --> 00:01:32.669
it comes to directing air traffic.

00:01:32.670 --> 00:01:34.529
Back in 2009,

00:01:34.530 --> 00:01:36.239
Reason produced a video about how

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:38.069
Canada and other countries

00:01:38.070 --> 00:01:40.469
had privatized air-traffic control

00:01:40.470 --> 00:01:42.389
and saw delays decrease

00:01:42.390 --> 00:01:44.159
in safety increase.

00:01:44.160 --> 00:01:46.169
Canadians allowed Nav Canada,

00:01:46.170 --> 00:01:48.149
a private company, to manage

00:01:48.150 --> 00:01:49.019
their skies.

00:01:49.020 --> 00:01:50.579
So the next time your plane is

00:01:50.580 --> 00:01:52.169
delayed, think about why you're

00:01:52.170 --> 00:01:53.009
stuck.

00:01:53.010 --> 00:01:54.959
Maybe it's because of the weather

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:57.659
or maybe it's because of politics.

00:01:57.660 --> 00:01:59.699
What would actually produce safer,

00:01:59.700 --> 00:02:01.589
cheaper and less disrupted air

00:02:01.590 --> 00:02:04.019
travel? More deregulation.

00:02:04.020 --> 00:02:05.819
Inflation adjusted ticket prices

00:02:05.820 --> 00:02:07.649
declined 60% between

00:02:07.650 --> 00:02:09.689
1980 and 2020, which

00:02:09.690 --> 00:02:11.489
explains how air travel went from

00:02:11.490 --> 00:02:12.989
something only businessmen and the

00:02:12.990 --> 00:02:15.719
wealthy did to a common practice.

00:02:15.720 --> 00:02:17.759
But too many aspects of air travel

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:19.589
remain under government's inept

00:02:19.590 --> 00:02:21.689
and stuck-in-the-past control.

00:02:21.690 --> 00:02:23.219
Foreign owned airlines are blocked

00:02:23.220 --> 00:02:24.509
from competing with domestic

00:02:24.510 --> 00:02:26.189
carriers in the name of national

00:02:26.190 --> 00:02:27.209
security.

00:02:27.210 --> 00:02:29.219
The number, placement and operation

00:02:29.220 --> 00:02:30.839
of airports are controlled by

00:02:30.840 --> 00:02:32.369
various levels of government,

00:02:32.370 --> 00:02:34.409
leading to insane monopolies

00:02:34.410 --> 00:02:36.299
and fewer flight options in

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:38.189
places such as Atlanta, Denver and

00:02:38.190 --> 00:02:39.299
Vegas.

00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:40.949
Even in today's less-than-free

00:02:40.950 --> 00:02:42.869
market, Southwest will have to

00:02:42.870 --> 00:02:44.609
fight like hell to win back

00:02:44.610 --> 00:02:46.649
customers by keeping prices low

00:02:46.650 --> 00:02:48.359
and performance high.

00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:50.219
The FAA and the government

00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:52.169
more generally doesn't face

00:02:52.170 --> 00:02:53.639
the same pressure.

00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:55.469
We'll see which one fixes

00:02:55.470 --> 00:02:57.149
its problems before the next

00:02:57.150 --> 00:02:58.409
Christmas travel season.

